/** @page ocrreleasehistory ocr Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section ocr_3_0 ocr Module Version 3.0
    - initial release
    - the trained data read from an explicit data directory given to
      @ref Qore::Ocr::TesseractEngine::constructor() "TesseractEngine::constructor()" is subject to the filesystem
      sandbox of the calling program: every trained data file Tesseract loads, including the sub-languages a
      trained data file names, must be allowed by the sandbox, and the language configuration in the trained data
      may only set the layout, segmentation and recognition parameters that the official trained data sets, so
      trained data cannot make Tesseract read or write another file; the system data directory is a system
      resource and is not checked
    - @ref Qore::Ocr::TesseractEngine "TesseractEngine" can be used by a program without filesystem access rights
      (\c PO_NO_FILESYSTEM) with the system data directory; an explicit data directory needs them and raises
      \c ILLEGAL-FILESYSTEM-ACCESS without them
    - a language code may only contain ASCII letters, digits, \c "_" and \c "-", and a data directory may not
      contain a NUL character, so that neither can name a file outside the data directory
*/
